<title>INDIA: India panel submits new companies draft bill.</title>
<headline>India panel submits new companies draft bill.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>A government-appointed panel submitted a new draft bill for companies to Indian finance minister P. Chidambaram on Thursday, the government said.</p>
<p>&quot;In the draft the working group has attempted a new corporate law which aims at striking a balance between the needs of the changing items and the need to ensure proper enforcement of corporate discipline,&quot; an official statement said.</p>
<p>The final draft which seeks to replace the Companies Act 1956 will be prepared after a public debate, it added.</p>
<p>--New Delhi newsroom +91-11-301-2024</p>
